Treat a missing mtab as nothing mounted under Cosmopolitan.

Windows has no /etc/mtab and mounts no ext filesystem, so tune2fs,
resize2fs and e2image refused every image with "Can't check if
filesystem is mounted due to missing mtab file". Same effect as
upstream's EXT2FS_NO_MTAB_OK.

--- a/lib/ext2fs/ismounted.c
+++ b/lib/ext2fs/ismounted.c
@@ -108,6 +108,10 @@
 
 	if ((f = setmntent (mtab_file, "r")) == NULL) {
 		if (errno == ENOENT) {
+#ifdef __COSMOPOLITAN__
+			/* Windows mounts no ext filesystem. */
+			return 0;
+#endif
 			if (ext2fs_safe_getenv("EXT2FS_NO_MTAB_OK"))
 				return 0;
 			else
